In article <wfRwPUa00YUo5=z5AT@andrew.cmu.edu>, peterb+@CMU.EDU (Peter Glen Berger) writes:

 > Anyway, a few quick suggestions, if anyone is still reading :-).
 > First, there is no rational reason that pets should be able to steal
 > from shops, unless the shopkeeper has an IQ of around room
 > temperature.  There should be only three ways to get things from
 > shops:  pay the shopkeeper, teleport out and deal with the Kops, or
 > kill the shopkeeper with good honest violence.  As it is, a lawful
 > character can use his pet to steal for him without pissing off his
 > God: this is wrong.
 > 
 > I'll post more later,
 > 
I don't think there is anything wrong with having the pet(s) steal for you.
After all, a shopkeeper can only watch one person (or monster) at a time,
so when he/she is watching you, the pet may get away with something.

This don't imbalance the game too much, as it is impossible to get a pet
to steal a specific item. (I haven't found a way to do it, at least.)
So it may go a long long time before you get a real good item for free,
I usually only get a few extra $ by selling stolen junk back to the shop.
I don't see why killing a peaceful shopkeeper or teleporting away would
be any 'better' than the pet trick for a lawful character.  It is
the pet that is doing the stealing, not you.  Perhaps there should be
a chance that the shopkeeper takes items from the pet when it tries
to escape, but it should still be possible.  It adds variation to 
the game. 
